   "is_new": true,
   "source": {
    "label": "thm:regret-safe",
    "number": "Theorem 3.2",
    "quote": "In the full-information setting without budget constraint, \\cref{alg:weight-pushing-stoc} runs in $O(|\\mathcal{V}|\\maxbid^2/\\epsilon^3)$ space and time per round. For $\\epsilon\\in(0,1)$ and any non-increasing sequence $\\{\\eta_t\\}_{t=1}^T$ with $\\eta_t>0$,\n\\[\n    \\mathsf{Reg}_{nb}(T) \\lesssim \\frac{\\maxbid\\log(1/\\epsilon)}{\\eta_T} + \\maxbid^2 \\sum_{t=1}^T \\eta_t \\,.\n\\]\nIf $\\eta_t = \\sqrt{\\tfrac{\\log 1/\\epsilon}{\\maxbid t}}, \\forall t$, then \n$\\mathsf{Reg}_{nb}(T)\\lesssim\\maxbid^{3/2}\\sqrt{T\\log 1/\\epsilon}$. Alternatively, if $\\eta_t = \\eta= \\sqrt{\\tfrac{\\log 1/\\epsilon}{\\maxbid T}}, \\forall t$, the same regret bound (up to constants) is also achieved."
   },
   "confidence": "high",
   "notes": "General bound M log(1/eps)/eta_T + M^2 sum eta_t also stated. Fixed-eta version (known T) gives same bound. Regret is against best stationary policy with expectation over contexts; competing bids fixed sequence. Theorem 5.1 shows an O(M^2/eps^3)-per-round implementation independent of |V| achieving the same bound."
  },
